\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Your profile looks less like a \'93type\'94 and more like a 
\f1\b set of tendencies that may interact differently depending on pressure, incentives, and workplace culture
\f0\b0 . In particular, the relatively high humility, empathy, and ethical-leadership scores are potentially important regulating capacities, while the Machiavellianism score is the clearest area where deliberate self-monitoring could be useful.\
One caveat: without knowing the questionnaire, its norms, scoring method, reliability, or whether scores are percentile-based, the numbers should be treated as 
\f1\b signals for reflection\'97not clinical or personality diagnoses
\f0\b0 .\
