\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Overall pattern\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 A reasonable working hypothesis would be:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \'93Principled and relatively humble leader who can also be strategically minded, with the greatest risk occurring when strategic thinking becomes overly instrumental under pressure.\'94
\f0\b0 \
Your empathy, humility and ethical-leadership scores could provide substantial counterweights to the more strategic aspects of your profile.\
The interesting question isn't 
\f2\i \'93Am I Machiavellian?\'94
\f0\i0  but rather:\

\f1\b When does strategic thinking help me lead effectively, and when might it tempt me to manage people, information, or relationships primarily as means to an outcome?
\f0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Possible workplace triggers\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 These aren't predictions, but useful hypotheses to test:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 High-stakes competition:
\f0\b0  promotion decisions, scarce resources, organisational politics or visible performance comparisons.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ambiguous authority:
\f0\b0  situations where nobody is clearly accountable and informal influence becomes important.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Perceived incompetence or unfairness:
\f0\b0  you may feel particularly motivated to take control when you believe the process is failing.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Time pressure:
\f0\b0  less time can mean less consultation and more reliance on your own strategic judgment.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Threat to an important objective:
\f0\b0  strong ethical intentions can sometimes coexist with rationalisations such as 
\f2\i \'93This is necessary to get the right result.\'94
\f0\i0 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Repeated interpersonal friction:
\f0\b0  even empathetic leaders can become more transactional when they feel someone is obstructing progress.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Context-sensitive risk points\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 The same behaviour can be adaptive in one context and harmful in another. Strategic political awareness can help you navigate a complex organisation; it becomes riskier if it involves 
\f1\b withholding relevant information, engineering outcomes without stakeholder awareness, using relationships instrumentally, or treating dissent primarily as an obstacle
\f0\b0 .\
Likewise, humility can be protective but can occasionally become excessive deference or reluctance to exercise authority when decisive leadership is genuinely required.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 2. Three behavioural risks to monitor\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1. Strategic thinking becoming overly instrumental\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Watch for:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 selectively sharing information because it improves your chances of getting an outcome;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 building alliances primarily for leverage;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 mentally categorising colleagues as \'93useful,\'94 \'93difficult,\'94 or \'93obstacles\'94;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 presenting a decision as more settled than it really is.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Monitor:
\f0\b0  
\f2\i \'93Would I consider this approach fair and transparent if someone affected by it could see the reasoning?\'94
\f0\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Moving too quickly from disagreement to control\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Under pressure, a capable and ethical leader can still conclude that 
\f2\i \'93I know what needs to happen; consultation is slowing us down.\'94
\f0\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Watch for:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 interrupting or shortening discussion;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 making decisions before dissenting views have been properly understood;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 becoming noticeably more directive with particular colleagues;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 interpreting disagreement as resistance rather than information.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Monitor:
\f0\b0  
\f2\i \'93Am I exercising appropriate authority, or am I reducing other people's agency unnecessarily?\'94
\f0\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 3. Ethical rationalisation under pressure\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Your high ethical-leadership score is encouraging, but self-perceived ethics are most informative when tested by difficult situations.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Watch for thoughts such as:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \'93It's for the greater good.\'94\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \'93They would understand if they knew the whole story.\'94\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \'93There isn't time to explain.\'94\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \'93This is technically allowed.\'94\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \'93Someone has to make the hard call.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 None automatically means you're doing something wrong. They are 
\f1\b pause signals
\f0\b0 .\
Ask: 
\f2\i \'93What would make this decision ethically uncomfortable if I were the person on the receiving end?\'94
\f0\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 3. Three strengths/protective capacities\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1. Humility \'97 82\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 This may be your strongest regulatory resource.\
Build on it by deliberately making room for correction, especially from people with less formal power. Humility is particularly valuable if you have strong strategic confidence because it creates a mechanism for detecting blind spots.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Use it actively:
\f0\b0 \
\'93What am I missing?\'94\uc0\u8232 \'93Who sees this differently?\'94\u8232 \'93What evidence would change my mind?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Ethical orientation \'97 79\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 This suggests a potentially strong internal commitment to responsible leadership.\
The next step is converting values into 
\f1\b decision processes
\f0\b0 , rather than relying solely on good intentions.\
For consequential decisions, establish simple rules such as:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Impact 
\f3\b0 \uc0\u8594 
\f1\b  Fairness 
\f3\b0 \uc0\u8594 
\f1\b  Transparency 
\f3\b0 \uc0\u8594 
\f1\b  Alternatives 
\f3\b0 \uc0\u8594 
\f1\b  Accountability
\f0\b0 \
That makes ethical behaviour more robust when you're tired, angry, rushed, or strongly invested in an outcome.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 3. Empathy \'97 64\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Empathy can regulate strategic behaviour by keeping the human consequences of decisions visible.\
One useful practice is 
\f1\b perspective-switching
\f0\b0 :\
\'93If I were the person with the least power in this situation, how would this decision look and feel?\'94\
Also distinguish empathy from agreement. You can understand someone's perspective while still making a difficult decision.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 4. A practical 4-week improvement plan\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Keep this deliberately small. The goal isn't to \'93fix\'94 your personality; it's to create better behavioural safeguards.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Week 1 \'97 Observe\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Micro-experiment:
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 For one week, notice moments involving conflict, competition, urgency or status. Don't try to change anything yet.\
After significant interactions, record:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What happened?\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What outcome did I want?\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What did I assume about the other person?\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Did I seek their perspective?\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Did I disclose enough relevant information?\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 How did my behaviour change under pressure?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Observable behaviour:
\f0\b0  Ask at least 
\f1\b one genuine question before advocating your preferred solution
\f0\b0  in a contentious discussion.\

\f1\b Reflection:
\f0\b0 \
\'93When did I feel most compelled to control the outcome?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Week 2 \'97 Add friction before important decisions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Choose two consequential decisions and introduce a 
\f1\b 10-minute ethical pause
\f0\b0  before acting.\
Ask:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Who benefits?\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Who bears the cost?\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Who hasn't been heard?\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What information am I tempted not to share?\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Would I be comfortable explaining my reasoning afterward?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Observable behaviour:
\f0\b0  Document the reasoning for at least one decision rather than relying solely on informal influence.\

\f1\b Reflection:
\f0\b0 \
\'93Did the pause change my decision, my confidence, or merely my explanation?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Week 3 \'97 Deliberately distribute power and credit\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Micro-experiment:
\f0\b0  In one meeting, deliberately invite a dissenting or less senior perspective before stating your own conclusion.\
Then give specific credit to someone whose contribution materially helped the outcome.\

\f1\b Observable behaviour:
\f0\b0  Use another person's name when describing their contribution rather than saying \'93we\'94 when individual attribution matters.\

\f1\b Reflection:
\f0\b0 \
\'93Whose contribution might have been invisible if I hadn't deliberately surfaced it?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Week 4 \'97 Feedback and repair\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Ask 
\f1\b two trusted colleagues
\f0\b0  for behavioural feedback.\
Don't ask:\
\'93Am I a good leader?\'94\
Ask something observable:\
\'93When we're under pressure, what is one thing I do that helps the team, and one thing I could do differently?\'94\
Look for recurring themes rather than defending yourself against individual comments.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Observable behaviour:
\f0\b0  If someone identifies a legitimate negative impact, acknowledge it without immediately explaining your intentions.\

\f1\b Reflection:
\f0\b0 \
\'93What feedback was hardest to hear, and why?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 5. Short scripts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Seeking feedback\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Direct
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93I'm working on how I lead under pressure. What's one behaviour I should keep doing, and one behaviour I could change?\'94\

\f1\b More specific
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93When I become focused on an outcome, do you notice me becoming too directive, dismissive, or controlling? I'd value a concrete example if so.\'94\

\f1\b After a difficult meeting
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93I'd like an honest read on my behaviour in that discussion. What did I do that helped, and where might I have made it harder for others to contribute?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Pausing before a reactive decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I'm inclined to decide this now, but I want ten minutes to check that I'm not reacting rather than reasoning.\'94\
\'93Before we act, what important perspective haven't we heard?\'94\
\'93I have a strong view, so I'd like to hear the strongest argument against it before I decide.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Giving credit\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I want to make sure [person/team] gets explicit credit here\'97their work on [specific contribution] materially improved the outcome.\'94\
\'93That was [person]'s idea originally, and my role was mainly helping us implement it.\'94\
\'93Before we move on, I don't want the contribution from [person/team] to get lost.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Repairing harm\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I've thought about what happened. My intention doesn't change the fact that my behaviour had an impact on you. I'm sorry.\'94\
\'93I was too forceful in that conversation and didn't give you enough room to contribute. I'd like to handle that differently next time.\'94\
\'93I don't want to defend the decision before understanding the impact. What would you like me to understand?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Responding ethically to conflict\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I disagree with the proposal, but I want to separate disagreement with the idea from judgment of the person.\'94\
\'93Let's make the disagreement explicit rather than trying to resolve it through informal influence.\'94\
\'93I still think we need to make this decision, but I want the reasoning and trade-offs to be transparent to the people affected.\'94\
\'93If there is a legitimate concern about fairness or harm, I don't want urgency to become an excuse for ignoring it.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 6. Questions to ask before applying any suggestion\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Context matters enormously. Before changing your behaviour, consider:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What is my actual authority here?
\f0\b0  Am I supposed to decide, facilitate, advise, or escalate?\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What are the legitimate constraints?
\f0\b0  Confidentiality, legal duties, safety, deadlines, commercial sensitivity, etc.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Could greater transparency itself create harm?
\f0\b0 \
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Am I mistaking healthy decisiveness for excessive control\'97or vice versa?
\f0\b0 \
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Does this workplace reward openness, or could particular disclosures create unnecessary interpersonal risk?
\f0\b0 \
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Who has less power than me in this situation?
\f0\b0 \
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Would I behave differently if my decision were publicly scrutinised?
\f0\b0 \
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Am I seeking feedback from people who can safely disagree with me?
\f0\b0 \
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Is this a genuine ethical concern, or simply discomfort because someone disagrees with me?
\f0\b0 \
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Could my attempt to be humble accidentally make accountability or decision-making unclear?
\f0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 One particularly useful test is:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \'93What would a reasonable, well-intentioned colleague who disagrees with me say I'm missing?\'94
\f0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 7. Final perspective\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 I'd avoid interpreting these numbers as evidence that you 
\f2\i are
\f0\i0  narcissistic, Machiavellian, psychopathic, sadistic, empathetic, humble, or ethical. They're questionnaire scores, not fixed identities.\
Your most useful takeaway may be the 
\f1\b interaction between the scores
\f0\b0 : relatively strong humility, empathy, and ethical orientation alongside a somewhat stronger strategic/transactional signal. Rather than trying to suppress strategic thinking, you can make it more accountable through transparency, perspective-taking, feedback, and deliberate pauses under pressure.\
And importantly, don't use your results to diagnose colleagues or explain their motives. 
\f1\b Use them as a private prompt for examining your own observable behaviour
\f0\b0 , while giving other people the same dignity, uncertainty, and privacy you'd want for yourself.\
If you'd like, I can also turn this into a 
\f1\b one-page leadership development worksheet or visual model
\f0\b0  you could use for your 4-week experiment.\
}